{"content":[{"c":["OPHRAH (P",{"c":["lace"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. City in Benjamin, probably identical with Ephraim (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.13.23","r":"2Sam.13.23","rawR":"2Sam.13.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.13.23","value":"2Sam.13.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 13:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.13.19","r":"2Chr.13.19","rawR":"2Chr.13.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.13.19","value":"2Chr.13.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 13:19"},", “Ephron”; ",{"href":"?bref=John.11.54","r":"John.11.54","rawR":"John.11.54","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.11.54","value":"John.11.54"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 11:54"},"). Ophrah is usually identified with the modern et-Taiyibeh, five miles (8 kilometers) north of Michmash and four miles (6.5 kilometers) northeast of Bethel."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. City in Manasseh owned by Gideon’s father, Joash the Abiezrite, and Gideon’s home (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.6.11","r":"Judg.6.11","rawR":"Judg.6.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.6.11","value":"Judg.6.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 6:11"},"). There the angel appeared to Gideon, commissioning him as God’s agent of relief from the Midianites (vv ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.6.12-24","r":"Judg.6.12-24","rawR":"Judg.6.12-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.6.12-24","value":"Judg.6.12-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"12-24"},"). Following his spectacular victory, Gideon was nominated for kingship, but he refused. Strangely, he constructed an ephod from the spoils of battle (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.8.22-28","r":"Judg.8.22-28","rawR":"Judg.8.22-28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.8.22-28","value":"Judg.8.22-28"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:22-28"},"), which Israel worshiped. The idol at Ophrah became a snare to Gideon and his family. Gideon died at Ophrah, an old man (vv ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.8.29-32","r":"Judg.8.29-32","rawR":"Judg.8.29-32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.8.29-32","value":"Judg.8.29-32"}],"t":"ref","v":"29-32"},"). His son Abimelech, ambitious for power, slaughtered his sibling rivals at Ophrah; only one of the 70, Jotham, escaped (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.9.1-6","r":"Judg.9.1-6","rawR":"Judg.9.1-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.9.1-6","value":"Judg.9.1-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:1-6"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"OphrahPlace","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Sm 13:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.13.23","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.13.23","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.13.23"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 13:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.13.19","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.13.19","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.13.19"},{"anchorText":"Jn 11:54","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.11.54","rawQueryValue":"John.11.54","sourceRefExact":"John.11.54"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 6:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.6.11","rawQueryValue":"Judg.6.11","sourceRefExact":"Judg.6.11"},{"anchorText":"12-24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.6.12-24","rawQueryValue":"Judg.6.12-24","sourceRefExact":"Judg.6.12-24"},{"anchorText":"8:22-28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.8.22-28","rawQueryValue":"Judg.8.22-28","sourceRefExact":"Judg.8.22-28"},{"anchorText":"29-32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.8.29-32","rawQueryValue":"Judg.8.29-32","sourceRefExact":"Judg.8.29-32"},{"anchorText":"9:1-6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.9.1-6","rawQueryValue":"Judg.9.1-6","sourceRefExact":"Judg.9.1-6"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"308451e7e78498e8e5fe54615a9dd74fcbf8c06e3d49da73c450de8fe1fcc6eb","sourceItemName":"OphrahPlace","sourceItemOrder":70,"sourceMember":"Articles/O.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"OphrahPlace","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Ophrah (Place)","title":"Ophrah (Place)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}